class:: WsGen
summary:: Waveset synthesis with per-waveset parameters
related:: Classes/WsMap, Classes/WsGendy
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic

description::
Generates a stream of wavesets. Each waveset is a positive half-cycle followed by a negative one. Length, peak, shape and the position of the middle zero crossing are read once at the start of each waveset, so demand-rate inputs such as link::Classes/Dbrown:: or link::Classes/Dseq:: advance one value per waveset.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Frequency of the waveset (1 / its length) in Hz.

argument:: amp
Peak amplitude of the waveset.

argument:: shape
Half-cycle shape: 0 sine, 1 triangle, 2 square, 3 spike. Fractional values morph between neighbours. The square has hard edges at the zero crossings and aliases.

argument:: skew
Position of the middle zero crossing, 0.01 to 0.99. 0.5 gives equal half-cycles.

argument:: repeats
How many times each waveset is played before new values are read.

argument:: glide
How far into each waveset the move from the previous values to the new ones takes, 0 to 1. 0 jumps at the zero crossing; 1 glides across the whole waveset. Repeated wavesets hold.

argument:: balance
Scales down the larger half-cycle so both halves enclose the same area, which removes the DC offset that skew and uneven halves produce, 0 (off) to 1 (equal area). Zero crossings and the peak stay where they are; the level drops as the halves become more uneven.

argument:: mul

argument:: add

method:: arTrig
Same as link::#*ar:: with one more argument, and returns code::[sig, trig]::. code::trig:: is a single-sample 1 at the start of the first waveset and then of every code::every::-th waveset (repeats count), so the waveset clock can drive other UGens.

argument:: every
Wavesets between triggers. Read each time the trigger fires, so a demand-rate input sets the number of wavesets until the next one.

examples::

code::
{ WsGen.ar(Dbrown(80, 900, 40), 0.3) ! 2 }.play;
::

code::
{ WsGen.ar(220, 0.3, MouseX.kr(0, 3), MouseY.kr(0.05, 0.95)) ! 2 }.play;
::

code::
{ WsGen.ar(Dwhite(60, 1200), Dwhite(0.05, 0.4), Dwhite(0, 3), Dwhite(0.1, 0.9)) ! 2 }.play;
::

code::
(
{
	WsGen.ar(
		Dseq([110, 220, 165, 330], inf),
		Dwhite(0.1, 0.4),
		Dwhite(0, 3),
		Dbrown(0.1, 0.9, 0.05),
		Dseq([8, 4, 16], inf)
	) ! 2
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	WsGen.ar(
		Dseq([Dseries(40, 7, 60), Dseries(460, -11, 38)], inf),
		0.3,
		Dseq([0, 1, 3], inf),
		Dseq([0.5, 0.2, 0.8], inf),
		Dwhite(1, 6)
	) ! 2
}.play;
)
::

code::
{ WsGen.ar(Dbrown(50, 400, 30), 0.3, 1, 0.5, Dwhite(2, 12), MouseX.kr(0, 1)) ! 2 }.play;
::

code::
{ WsGen.ar(Dwhite(40, 2000), 0.25, Dwhite(0, 3), Dwhite(0.1, 0.9), 1, 1) ! 2 }.play;
::

code::
(
{
	var freq = Dseq([Dshuf([55, 82.5, 110, 165, 220], 4), Dwhite(800, 3000, 40)], inf);
	WsGen.ar(freq, Dbrown(0.05, 0.35, 0.05), Dbrown(0, 3, 0.4), Dbrown(0.05, 0.95, 0.1), Dwhite(1, 20), Dwhite(0, 1)) ! 2
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	var rate = LFNoise1.kr(0.2).exprange(0.5, 40);
	var freq = Dbrown(30, 600, Dwhite(5, 60));
	Pan2.ar(WsGen.ar(freq, 0.3, LFNoise2.kr(rate).range(0, 3), LFNoise2.kr(rate).range(0.05, 0.95)), LFNoise1.kr(1))
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	var n = 5;
	Splay.ar(Array.fill(n, { |i|
		WsGen.ar(Dbrown(40 * (i + 1), 300 * (i + 1), 20), 0.5 / n.sqrt, i % 4, Dwhite(0.2, 0.8), Dwhite(1, 30), 0.5)
	}))
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	var src = WsGen.ar(Dseq([Dgeom(30, 1.07, 70)], inf), 0.4, Dseq([2, 3], inf), Dwhite(0.05, 0.95));
	LeakDC.ar(RLPF.ar(src, LFNoise1.kr(0.3).exprange(200, 5000), 0.2)) * 0.3 ! 2
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	var trig = Impulse.kr(2);
	var freq = Demand.kr(trig, 0, Dseq([55, 73.4, 98, 130.8], inf));
	WsGen.ar(freq, Decay2.kr(trig, 0.01, 0.4) * 0.4, Dwhite(0, 2), Dwhite(0.3, 0.7)) ! 2
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	var sig, trig;
	#sig, trig = WsGen.arTrig(Dbrown(40, 200, 10), 0.3, 1, Dwhite(0.2, 0.8), Dwhite(1, 8), every: 24);
	Pan2.ar(sig, TRand.ar(-1, 1, trig))
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	var sig, trig;
	#sig, trig = WsGen.arTrig(Dbrown(30, 120, 5), 0.25, 0, 0.5, 1, 0, 0, Dseq([3, 5, 8, 13], inf));
	sig + Ringz.ar(trig, Demand.ar(trig, 0, Dseq([800, 1200, 1800, 2700], inf)), 0.08, 0.1) ! 2
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	var sig, trig;
	#sig, trig = WsGen.arTrig(Dwhite(60, 400), 0.4, Dwhite(0, 3), Dwhite(0.1, 0.9), Dwhite(1, 4), 0, 1, 12);
	LeakDC.ar(RLPF.ar(sig, Demand.ar(trig, 0, Dwhite(200, 6000)).lag(0.01), 0.3)) * 0.4 ! 2
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	var trig = WsGen.arTrig(Dseq([2, 3, 4, 6], inf), 0, every: 1)[1];
	var follow = WsGen.ar(Latch.ar(TExpRand.ar(80, 900, trig), trig), 0.3, Dwhite(0, 3), Dwhite(0.2, 0.8));
	follow ! 2
}.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
	var sig, trig;
	#sig, trig = WsGen.arTrig(Dseq([Dseries(30, 4, 50)], inf), 0.3, 3, 0.5, 2, every: Dwhite(4, 40));
	sig * EnvGen.ar(Env.perc(0.002, TRand.ar(0.01, 0.2, trig)), trig) * 2 ! 2
}.play;
)
::

code::
{ WsGen.ar(Dbrown(60, 300, 20), 0.4, 0, MouseX.kr(0.05, 0.95), 1, 0, MouseY.kr(0, 1)) ! 2 }.play;
::
